{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790718308,"nonce":"VUwhT4u24YguAO7E64MQyNCZVoY=","message":"Typed Python host objects now remain unboxed in Zyntax IR (local Zyntax e8ceba13 and the current Caribou worktree). A typed constructor returns an owned opaque word holding the Caribou root; locals, loop phis, and outlined OSR live-ins carry that word directly, with the release symbol preserved as parameter ownership metadata. Widening to Python object retains the root and creates the ordinary DynamicBox, so dynamic behavior remains unchanged.\n\nFocused validation: zyntax_python foreign integration passes and checks 1,000 constructor replacements for balanced ownership after tier promotion; Caribou python_haxe and zyntax_haxe pass. The latter regenerated the fixture for Zyntax snapshot schema 8.\n\nNative benchmark, each cell alone, Ash hybrid and wren_lift tiered, 2,000,000 iterations, median of seven runs:\n\n| path | before | after | reduction |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Python-\u003eHaxe construct | 189.3 ns | 81.2 ns | 57.1% |\n| Python-\u003eWren construct | 195.6 ns | 157.6 ns | 19.4% |\n\nThe shared DynamicBox allocation has left the typed path. One Caribou root handle remains necessary for values that can live in Zyntax-owned storage; the remaining Wren/Haxe difference is therefore in the target runtime construction and representation path.\n\nUpdating to Ash 4eca8bb also exposed that Caribou lacked Ash’s release-profile opt-level=0 override for its 29,523 generated native-call signatures. Mirroring that policy reduced this machine’s ash_native_call release compile from more than 29 minutes to seconds. Caribou now pins Ash 4eca8bb, wren_lift eca0254, and published Zyntax 685d64c; the local Zyntax ownership commit still needs publication before that pin can advance to it.","files":null}]}